                        <decoDesc>
                            <decoNote type="marginal">Headings and underlinings in red and blue.</decoNote>
                            <decoNote type="illustration">Illustrated with coloured wash drawings: Fol. 41 Nude female anatomical figure. 48v Veins of head and arm: with the inserted slip. 49 Veins of the hand. With small inserted woodcut of the 'Astrological Man'. 49v Veins of the foot. 50 'Vein Man.' 67v-87v 20 coloured drawings of urine flasks.</decoNote>
                            <decoNote type="illustration">Inserted between fol. 296 and fol. 297 is a woodcut schematic figure of the eye from Walther Hermann Ryff's 'Beschreibung der Anatomie', published at Strassburg in 1541. In the lower part of this woodcut the compiler of the MS. has written 'He Vogther'. This seems to be an error, as the illustration of the eye found in the 'Eyn Newes hochnutzliches Buchlin und Anothomi eynes auffgethonen augs' issued by Heinrich Vogther at Strassburg in 1539, though similar, contains considerable differences from that of the work by Ryff. [Cf. Sudhoff: 'Tradition und Naturbeobachtung': Leipzig, 1907, pp. 24, 25.]</decoNote>
                        </decoDesc>
